# AI engineering lifecycle

Uncoil is most useful when the same run can move through the whole improvement loop:

1. [Instrument the agent](/docs/observability) with spans, sessions, costs, and prompt versions.
2. [Inspect](/docs/trace-anatomy) timelines, payloads, failures, and quality signals.
3. Build [evaluators](/docs/evaluation) and [datasets](/docs/datasets) from representative traces.
4. [Compare prompt and model candidates](/docs/release-gates) against the same dataset.
5. Promote only after the [release gate](/docs/release-gates) passes, then monitor production drift.

Stable trace and project identifiers keep each decision connected to its evidence.

## Next steps

- [Send your first trace](/docs/quickstart) to start the loop.
- [Read a trace](/docs/trace-anatomy) from its root span down to the failed step.
- [Build a dataset](/docs/datasets) from the traces you want to test against.
